# Stanley Reference Designs

Use this skill when the user asks for a more modern, premium, Apple-like, Wise-like, Stripe-like, Webflow-like, or generally better website design.

Do not copy another brand literally. Extract principles and transform them into Stanley Systems' own warm, money-first, service-business design language.

## Reference principles

### Apple-style principles

Use:
- cinematic whitespace
- oversized confident type
- one dominant idea per viewport
- minimal chrome
- restrained motion
- high contrast between headline and canvas
- careful vertical rhythm

Avoid:
- generic centered emptiness
- product imagery if none exists
- black sections for Stanley Systems

### Wise-style principles

Use:
- direct money-first headlines
- friendly confidence
- bold green accent
- plain-language conversion flow
- clear numbers only when they are meaningful

Avoid:
- cartoonish treatment
- copying Wise's exact palette, layout, or brand forms

### Stripe/Webflow/Framer-style principles

Use:
- polished section rhythm
- crisp surface treatment
- subtle gradients or linework only when they support the story
- strong responsive composition
- meaningful interactive states

Avoid:
- purple tech gradients
- fake product dashboards
- complex visual systems that service-business owners will not understand

### Notion/Cal.com-style principles

Use:
- restrained neutral palette
- utility and clarity
- clean cards only when useful
- low visual noise

Avoid:
- making the site too plain or under-designed

## Stanley transformation rule

Every reference must be translated through Stanley Systems constraints:

- warm off-white canvas
- navy text
- Stanley green accent
- money, time, owner relief
- service-business clarity
- no AI-first language
- no dark-mode tech aesthetic
- no generic SaaS filler

## How to apply this skill

Before designing, choose one primary reference posture and one secondary support posture.

Examples:
- Hero: Apple whitespace plus Wise money clarity.
- Explainer section: Stripe rhythm plus Stanley green revenue-flow visual.
- Package section: Webflow polish plus Notion restraint.
- Calculator flow: Wise clarity plus Cal.com utility.

Then state the chosen posture briefly in implementation notes or your final report.
